      "id": 1,
      "text": "Entertainer Marie Osmond says her paternal great-great-grandfather founded the community of Osmond, Wyoming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osmond%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Osmond was originally called Dry Creek and later Mount Pleasant before being renamed in honor of George Osmond in 1901.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/osmond_wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Many early residents of Osmond had Swedish ancestry, leading the community to be occasionally known as Sweden.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/osmond_wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Henderson family established a foothold in Osmond in 1885, initially living in a tent before building a log house.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/osmond_wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The U.S. government briefly prospected for vanadium in Osmond during the 1940s, digging a four-hundred-foot tunnel in 1949.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/osmond_wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Osmond sits on a flat valley floor bordered by the Salt River Range and the Wyoming Range mountains.",
